# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
ODYSSEY_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-me-with-a-long-random-string

# Optional: bind to a specific LXC IP instead of all interfaces. Leave unset
# in compose to bind 0.0.0.0 (fine if the LXC itself is LAN-only).
# BIND_IP=10.0.0.50

# Optional: split-mount for hybrid local-rootfs + NAS storage. Leave both
# unset in local dev (compose uses ./_data and ./_data/audio).
# On Proxmox/LXC: ODYSSEY_DATA_HOST_DIR points at a local-rootfs dir
# (holds episodes.db + import/), and ODYSSEY_AUDIO_HOST_DIR points at
# the CIFS-mounted NAS audio catalog. The second bind layers on top of
# the first at /data/audio inside the container.
# ODYSSEY_DATA_HOST_DIR=/opt/archive-service/_data
# ODYSSEY_AUDIO_HOST_DIR=/data/audio

# Optional: expose this service to friends over the public internet via a
# Cloudflare Tunnel + Access. See archive-service/CLOUDFLARE.md for the
# one-time dashboard setup. Paste the tunnel token from
# Cloudflare → Zero Trust → Networks → Tunnels → Connect → Docker. When
# this is set, scripts/up.sh starts the `cloudflared` sidecar; LAN and
# Tailscale access keep working independently.
# CLOUDFLARED_TUNNEL_TOKEN=eyJ...
